<title>RUSSIA: Russia's IMB gets $50 mln syndicated loan.</title>
<headline>Russia's IMB gets $50 mln syndicated loan.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group of U.S., European and Japanese banks, led by Chase Manhattan Ltd, extended a one-year, $50 million loan to one of Russia's biggest banks, International Moscow Bank (IMB), IMB said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The credit was priced at 3.55 percent over LIBOR, IMB said in a statement.</p>
<p>It is the first syndicated loan for the bank, it said.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
